Lord Windgrace in BGR, built to Bracket 3 rules. This guide is a starting point generated from the decklist — the sections below group what the deck actually contains by what each card is there to do.

# The commander
Lord Windgrace :: +2: Discard a card, then draw a card. If a land card is discarded this way, draw an additional card.

# Game Changers (3 of 3)
Crop Rotation :: As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a land.
Field of the Dead :: This land enters tapped.
The One Ring :: When The One Ring enters, if you cast it, you gain protection from everything until your next turn.

# Removal you can point anywhere
Vandalblast :: Destroy target artifact you don't control.
Assassin's Trophy :: Destroy target permanent an opponent controls. Its controller may search their library for a basic land card, put it…
Terminate :: Destroy target creature. It can't be regenerated.
Beast Within :: Destroy target permanent. Its controller creates a 3/3 green Beast creature token.
Windgrace's Judgment :: For any number of opponents, destroy target nonland permanent that player controls.

# Card advantage
Constant Mists :: Buyback—Sacrifice a land.
Life from the Loam :: Return up to three target land cards from your graveyard to your hand.
Cultivate :: Search your library for up to two basic land cards, reveal those cards, put one onto the battlefield tapped and the…
Kodama's Reach :: Search your library for up to two basic land cards, reveal those cards, put one onto the battlefield tapped and the…
Phyrexian Arena :: At the beginning of your upkeep, you draw a card and you lose 1 life.
Harmonize :: Draw three cards.

# Recursion
Splendid Reclamation :: Return all land cards from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped.
World Shaper :: Whenever this creature attacks, you may mill three cards.
Titania, Protector of Argoth :: When Titania enters, return target land card from your graveyard to the battlefield.
